any vaccine so far because the mother had believed it is more natural, but she was a little concerned after she read
in an article that vaccination is beneficial for children. You explain to her the benefits of the child being vaccinated. At
the end, she decides not to vaccinate her child. Which one of the following is the most appropriate approach in this
situation?','{"A":"Inform child protection services.","B":"Call the police as she is putting the baby’s health at risk.","C":"Inform the local community council.","D":"Respect her decision.","E":"Apply for guardianship to the guardianship court."}','D','According to current regulations in Australia, vaccination is not compulsory and parents can choose not to vaccinate
their children. Physicians are required to fully explain the benefits and risks of vaccination to parents, and respect
their wishes if they refuse vaccination of their children.
Any option suggesting reporting of such parents to authorities such as child protection services, police, court, etc is
incorrect.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"990","duplicate_group_id":"exact-15b11ba51338","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6a3a86545d6401898065","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":401,"source_qid":"990"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"6a3a86545d6401898065","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":401,"source_qid":"990","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A mother brings her 6-month-old daughter for advice regarding vaccination of her baby. The child has not received\nany vaccine so far because the mother had believed it is more natural, but she was a little concerned after she read\nin an article that vaccination is beneficial for children. You explain to her the benefits of the child being vaccinated. At\nthe end, she decides not to vaccinate her child. Which one of the following is the most appropriate approach in this\nsituation?","options":{"A":"Inform child protection services.","B":"Call the police as she is putting the baby’s health at risk.","C":"Inform the local community council.","D":"Respect her decision.","E":"Apply for guardianship to the guardianship court."},"source_answer":"D","source_explanation":"According to current regulations in Australia, vaccination is not compulsory and parents can choose not to vaccinate\ntheir children. Physicians are required to fully explain the benefits and risks of vaccination to parents, and respect\ntheir wishes if they refuse vaccination of their children.\nAny option suggesting reporting of such parents to authorities