step if verbal de-escalating fails. However, the situation with Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders
is different. Aboriginal hospital experience can be very stressful for Aboriginals and also
bewildering for health workers.
In such cases, Aboriginal and Torres Strait islander hospital liaison officers (IHLO’s) play an
important role in making rapport and building relationship with Aboriginal patients. Therefore, it is
strongly recommended that prior to any physical restraining or contacting the police, the IHLO or
Aboriginal health worker is contacted to be present and de-escalate the situation.
The main reason for such necessity is the cultural differences and the familiarity of Aboriginal
health workers with the background and sensitivities of this group. For example, while a caring eye
contact is usually perceived as empathy from an aggressive patient, it is unacceptable and
provoking for Aboriginal Australians.
The security staff also must be present in case they are needed but no intervention should take
place as long as possible, and until the Aboriginal health worker takes over.
Other options may be considered after appropriate intervention by and advice from an IHLO or
Aboriginal health worker.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"1592","duplicate_group_id":"exact-3adf7aee5378","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9a96f75e2ebca1cdf7a1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":460,"source_qid":"1592"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
