pubic tubercle, in contrast to inguinal hernias that present as a swelling medial to the pubic tubercle.
Most of the time, the diagnosis is evident by physical exam; however, in situations when the physical exam is uncertain, such as in obese patients, additional imaging studies are recommended. Ultrasonography of the groin region is particularly
useful if confusion exists as to the location of the hernia.
This is particularly important owing to the fact that femoral hernias are approached differently from inguinal hernias. While watchful waiting may be an option for asymptomatic or minimally symptomatic inguinal hernia, this is not recommended for
femoral hernias due to the high risk of complications.
(Option A) Ultrasonography is used when the diagnosis is uncertain clinically. ​CT scan is used if ultrasound results are equivocal and non-diagnostic. MRI has the highest accuracy but is not readily available and cost-effective.
(Option C) Femora hernias have a high rate of incarceration and strangulation and it is unlikely that an incarcerated femoral hernia resolves with bowel rest.
(Options D and E) The diagnosis is certain in this case scenario. Fine needle or excisioanl biopsies are not necessary when hernia is suspected.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"898","duplicate_group_id":"exact-859ce4a24e44","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8f32ddbb7fe3f76fd9b6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":548,"source_qid":"898"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
